{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"152","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Garden"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya has a very beautiful country garden that can be represented as an "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" rectangular field divided into "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n·m"},{"kind":"text","text":" squares. One beautiful day Vasya remembered that he needs to pave roads between "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" important squares that contain buildings. To pave a road, he can cover some squares of his garden with concrete."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each garden square we know number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aij"},{"kind":"text","text":" that represents the number of flowers that grow in the square with coordinates "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"text","text":". When a square is covered with concrete, all flowers that grow in the square die."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya wants to cover some squares with concrete so that the following conditions were fulfilled: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" important squares should necessarily be covered with concrete "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" from each important square there should be a way to any other important square. The way should go be paved with concrete-covered squares considering that neighboring squares are squares that have a common side "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the total number of dead plants should be minimum "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As Vasya has a rather large garden, he asks you to help him."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first input line contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n·m ≤ 200"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ k ≤ min(n·m, 7"},{"kind":"text","text":")) — the garden's sizes and the number of the important squares. Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"aij"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ aij ≤ 1000"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the numbers of flowers in the squares. Next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain coordinates of important squares written as \""},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without quotes) ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ x ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ y ≤ m"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The numbers written on one line are separated by spaces. It is guaranteed that all "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" important squares have different coordinates."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first line print the single integer — the minimum number of plants that die during the road construction. Then print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines each containing "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters — the garden's plan. In this plan use character \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"X"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (uppercase Latin letter X) to represent a concrete-covered square and use character \".\" (dot) for a square that isn't covered with concrete. If there are multiple solutions, print any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 3 2\n1 2 3\n1 2 3\n1 2 3\n1 2\n3 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"9\n.X.\n.X.\n.XX\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 5 4\n1 4 5 1 2\n2 2 2 2 7\n2 4 1 4 5\n3 2 1 7 1\n1 1\n1 5\n4 1\n4 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"26\nX..XX\nXXXX.\nX.X..\nX.XX.\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"152E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/152/problem/E"}